%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ad7235ffe8a815c4eb369fe572eb183f, type: 3}
  m_Name: JournalSettings
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: SafeHaven::JournalSettings
  backstory:
  - group: The old world
    title: The Pact
    line: What people and forest once promised
    body: 'Long ago, people promised to leave the forest enough room to live. Its guardians promised in return to keep older, hungrier things at bay.


      Nobody living can say when that ended. Some say the pact was broken. Others say it was only forgotten, which may be worse. The trails went first, then the villages, and the forest began to take memories along with the wildlife and the people.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: be9b38a6d1e80f04b9412f36fe351069, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The old world
    title: What the Forest Does
    line: It doesn't kill the lost
    body: 'The forest does not kill the lost. It forgets them.


      First the way home goes, then their names, and then there is nobody left to find. People who come back from deep in the trees talk about it the way you talk about a dream going as you wake. Ingrid kept herself by saying one word over and over so it couldn''t be taken.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 00e21ff059394a4459d8cec92bc2d489, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4309b569c79f91447abd766ead239143, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The old world
    title: The Hearth
    line: The one thing it cannot forget
    body: 'A hearth that someone tends is the one thing the forest cannot forget.


      That was the old bargain, as far as anyone can make it out. People kept a fire beside the portal and the portal kept the night from their door. No fire had burned there in a hundred winters when you woke beside those stones.


      So this is not a base for its own sake. Each fire feeds the ward and carries further through the mist. The lost can see it and know which way is home.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f89173a9aeb790c4f9aeb1cc56e0e655, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c89a5bcf92e164347b7e6ec84e091158, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The old world
    title: The Portal
    line: An old thing, and awake
    body: 'At the heart of the clearing stand cracked old stones, warm to the touch. They are not quite a door and not quite a person.


      The portal''s ward still shelters one clearing, strong enough for daily peace and not much more. Where the old pact has cracked, things can push through, and you will usually hear about it first. It speaks when it has something to say. It is worth listening, and worth remembering that it has its own reasons for wanting a fire lit.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 00e21ff059394a4459d8cec92bc2d489, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 084db206456f42e46a331a84e1af59f6, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The expedition
    title: Seven Went In
    line: Why anyone came here
    body: 'The expedition came for four of its own, and to look into rumours of a bewitched forest.


      Sigrid led it. Eirik carried a soldier''s sense of where a wall is weakest and Runa could read a trail two days old. Ahead of them had gone Ingrid the alchemist, Bjarne the smith, Tor the carpenter and Liv, who reads runes and would rather be right than safe.


      You walked with them. By noon it was the middle of the night.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 55b4e1172114b804ca7eeca9d56c0489, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The expedition
    title: The Day the Stones Broke
    line: How you came to be alone
    body: 'Something very large came through the trees, and the only way left was the old waystones. Sigrid knew the passage. You held the creatures back while the connection woke, and it opened badly.


      When the stones broke they threw everyone in a different direction. You were the one the portal caught, and you woke on quiet grass with nobody beside you.


      Liv says the stones broke along a line, and that this matters. Nobody has yet got her to say why.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a089752e48d75934fb5e34dbeec0b389, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2dbe96364a9b5f045b67fd500c07b820, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The expedition
    title: Ingrid's Word
    line: The first to come home
    body: 'She lay under a root for three nights watching your fire and saying the word so the forest couldn''t have it. Fire. Fire. Fire.


      Ingrid knows more about the curse than she lets on. She saw Bjarne thrown north when the stones broke, towards the troll country. The rest she couldn''t see.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f7e615034e347bc438f7fdf1f08bd615, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 549b1d6c09f61624db2b6d1ca1e75e16, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The old world
    title: The Boundary Stones
    line: Where the pact's land ended
    body: 'When the pact was kept, people did not only tend a hearth beside the portal. They walked the land the pact gave them, and where it ended they set tall stones and lit them from that fire.


      A lit stone said that this much of the forest remembered a hearth. Inside the ring nobody lost the way home, and nobody lost their name.


      When the hearth went cold the stones went cold one by one, and the forest took back what they had held: the roads, the villages and everyone on them. The stones are still out there past the meadows, waiting for a hand that keeps a fire.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bb2c787a2de76634ba9260ee402850fc, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e44f24c818bfcfc4c9063f56bf4b521a, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The forest's own
    title: The Guardians
    line: What was set to keep the woods
    body: 'The Root Guardians were not always hostile. They were set to keep the forest, on the forest''s side of the old promise, and they are still doing it. Whatever twisted them did not tell them to stop.


      That is the uncomfortable part. Nothing you meet on the root paths thinks it has done anything wrong.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f66a8d86463697438ce75621f51e12d, type: 2}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c3b37904069014841a0dcd346c26acd2, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The forest's own
    title: The First of Them
    line: Grown vast under its hollow
    body: 'The Heartroot was the first of the guardians. It has grown old and enormous under its hollow, keeping a forest that is no longer there to be kept.


      Nobody has told it. It is not at all clear that it could be told.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d0d3ffee305a6ca489fca58781bf31c1, type: 2}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7a61a48f6e3663244a3ffc24f4680a9e, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The forest's own
    title: Troll Country
    line: North, where the valleys start
    body: 'Trolls are older than the road and pay it no attention. The small ones throw stones and hold grudges. The old ones walk the same round for longer than anyone has kept count, with moss and whole trees growing on their shoulders, and they smell you long before they see you.


      Stories say a troll can be bargained with, if you have something it wants and the nerve to stand still. This journal does not recommend finding out.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 916ab17a0415c3041aec1267259d1567, type: 2}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0f8550ed498e12241a3a12a44e3bb053, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The forest's own
    title: The Barrow Dead
    line: Still in their mail
    body: 'Whoever lies in the barrows was buried with honour once, and in good iron. The draugar don''t remember the honour. They remember the iron, and the wall they stood in, and they go on standing in it.


      They are slow and patient and hard to stop. The old stories say fire ends them.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 18c8362f09cf64a468e9ae4ae6d4422b, type: 2}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4b229cbf90a12f344ba05af46771aeb5, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The people
    title: Sigrid
    line: Leader of the expedition
    body: 'Sigrid has led people through worse country than most of them know about, and it shows mostly in what Sigrid doesn''t say. It was her voice in the stones. She knew the old passage before any of you reached it, and she has not said how.


      She was carried out of the woods with a wound she treats as a scheduling problem. Ask her about the expedition and you get the facts in order. Ask who taught her to read waystones and the subject changes.


      While she is home a raid gives you half a minute more: she has told you plainly how long you really have, and you believe her.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b230d041259b863428e4e973c6ff0d86, type: 2}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d44ee5592bb9a2c4aa2953eb4fab1ad7, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The people
    title: Eirik
    line: Soldier and warden
    body: 'Eirik was a soldier and has never entirely stopped. The first thing asked on seeing the Haven was where the wall was weakest, which at the time was all of it.


      You found Eirik fighting, and it took a moment to tell whether help was wanted. Don''t expect thanks. Expect to be told about your footwork.


      With Eirik on the wall the ward holds half as long again in a breach. No one has explained how a person can make a ward stubborn, and Eirik sees no need to.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 33e7204287863854f8c6ad025490f531, type: 2}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 226878f3b74cac74f92744bfe07aca7f, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The people
    title: Runa
    line: Tracker
    body: 'Runa reads a trail two days old and counts her arrows when she lends them. She left marks in the woods that only show after dark, for people she wasn''t sure were still coming, and she followed them home herself when you came.


      She doesn''t like how the forest has started moving. She doesn''t like how the boar looked that first morning either, and has never said what she thinks it meant.


      With Runa at home every briefing has one more rumour in it. She hears them from somewhere. It''s better not to ask how far she walks at night.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4260d606f7c62c042b848adc806c44d3, type: 2}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 597886e2642f88c4eab3fc52a1e60eb4, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The people
    title: Bjarne
    line: Smith
    body: 'The stones threw Bjarne north, into troll country, and he stayed alive there by being too much trouble to eat. He has a low opinion of your anvil. He''d have a low opinion of any anvil he hadn''t made.


      He talks about the trolls with more respect than he talks about most people. He says he struck a bargain with one and won''t say what it was for.


      With Bjarne home the forge works faster and repairs cost half. He hates seeing a good edge go to waste, and he hates it loudly.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 11400000, guid: de521ad7beeb20b49878a9b40c96bced, type: 2}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cebe443fe120590438073ac16c885b26, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The people
    title: Tor
    line: Carpenter
    body: 'Tor had to be cut out of the roots, and came out asking who had built your hearth, because it was crooked. It was. Tor went and fixed it before sitting down.


      Tor doesn''t say much about the time in the roots, except that they are very slow and very patient, and that wood remembers being a tree for longer than you would like.


      With Tor home the sawbench works faster, and mending the Haven after a breach costs half.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 11400000, guid: df34e8e1df8ff0241a216bfddf9b631c, type: 2}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 34f6a519f6c1b304094d0d38d7c6689a, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: The people
    title: Liv
    line: Rune scholar
    body: 'Liv reads runes, and would rather be right than safe. You found her in a ring of stones she had laid herself, still taking notes. She had not eaten for some time and was annoyed at being interrupted.


      She says the stones broke along a line and that this matters. She has told you why three times now, and you are nearly sure each explanation was different. She doesn''t seem to think that''s a problem.


      Liv is the only one who knows the raid runes, and with her home the cauldron works faster too.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8adfc30233928ec499c01587419eabaa, type: 2}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a68b4df3b2228c44aa638d42833cedec, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: A Letter, Unsent
    line: Folded small, in a dry tin
    body: 'Dear Sister. They say the road is good as far as the second ford, and that I shall be home before the barley. The people here are kind, though they keep asking me what I am called.


      I told them. I am sure I told them.


      The rest of it is the same three lines, written over and over in a hand that gets worse.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: da47952fda29d084cbe75b901262741f, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: Liv's Notes on the Stones
    line: Her hand, and three different inks
    body: 'Waystones broke along a line, not at random. Line runs from the portal to the third barrow to somewhere north I can''t get to.


      If I am right, the stones were never meant to carry people. They carry the promise, and people are what falls off.


      Sigrid will ask if that helps. It does not help. It is still true.


      Later, and shakier: Stay in the ring. Stay in the ring until someone comes, and do not answer anything that uses your name.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f7acd31b0d110644cb72c5789d2250b5, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: The Last Smith's Note
    line: Scratched on a rusted plate
    body: 'To the next one at this anvil. Keep the fire in. I don''t mean the forge. I mean the one by the stones, the one that matters. I let it go out one winter because I had work on and I thought a night wouldn''t hurt.


      I can''t now remember what it was I was making.


      The iron from the barrows is good. Don''t take it from anyone who is still using it.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5aa62c88656ebf340ab5a9d8dabf5a22, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: A Waystone Rubbing
    line: Charcoal on birch bark
    body: 'Someone pressed bark against a stone and rubbed it with charcoal until the marks came up. Beside it, in a careful hand, is a guess at the meaning.


      We keep the fire. You keep the dark.

      We leave the old trees. You leave the door.

      Whoever forgets first owes the other everything.


      The guess has been crossed out, and under it someone has written: not a guess.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 10e0ae7a661139940994890c891d05a9, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: The Lost Man's Song
    line: A children's counting song, on a torn page
    body: 'One for the road and two for the ford,

      Three for the wolf and four for the lord,

      Five for the name that you gave at the door,

      Six for the one who won''t ask any more.


      Seven''s the fire. Don''t say what it''s for.

      Seven''s the fire. Say it once more.


      Every village south of the river knows this one, and nobody there can tell you where it comes from.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8ce0b158af6046c41956e616f0e2e711, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: The Troll Toll
    line: A trader's list, much handled
    body: 'What the old one on the north road will take, as far as I have found:


      A whole cheese: no.

      A good knife: looked at it and gave it back.

      A song: stayed to hear the end, then hit the cart.

      A stone, carried from a long way off, and told where it came from: let us by.


      They say it collects them. I say it misses somewhere. Don''t run, and don''t lie about the stone.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c00416e61ff33349a28fc7fde039531, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: Barrow Inscription
    line: Copied from a door lintel
    body: 'HERE STOOD THE WALL AT THE NORTH GATE. THEY DID NOT GIVE WAY.


      Below it, in smaller and much later letters:


      Nobody has told them it is over. We tried. Bring fire and don''t stand where they are looking.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 94d913258f8068a449d54e66787c7bc3, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: The Hearth Law
    line: A page from an old rule of the house
    body: 'Let the hearth be tended by whoever is nearest, and let no one say it was another''s turn.


      Let no one be turned away from it, for you do not know whose name they have lost.


      Let the fire be fed before the household, in hard winters and in good ones, and let it be told each night who is home and who is not, so that it may go on looking for them.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7aee147a37d03104fbb95a90aaba2d27, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: A Tally on Bark
    line: Notches, and one word
    body: 'A long strip of bark, cut with neat rows of notches in fives. Whoever kept it counted days for a long time. The rows get crooked about two thirds of the way along, and after that the notches stop being in fives.


      At the very end, cut deep: FIRE.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fd049309f7114524fac3de4f7f65ca31, type: 3}
    summary: 
  - group: Found in the woods
    title: Something Runa Left
    line: Tied to a branch with a bit of red cord
    body: 'A scrap with marks on it that only make sense after dark, when you can see which way the moss glows. Runa''s way of leaving a trail for someone she expected to come after her.


      There''s a line at the bottom, in plain letters, as if she had thought better of being clever.


      If you''re reading this and you aren''t one of mine, take the left fork anyway. The right one isn''t there in the morning.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 1
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fc10e401fb174e54887378e64aa6ee77, type: 3}
    summary: 
  mechanics:
  - group: Getting about
    title: Your Windows
    line: What each key opens
    body: '(B) your bag and what you can make by hand

      (C) your character and what you wear

      (K) your abilities and the skill bar

      (N) your skills and perks

      (H) the Haven, from anywhere in it

      (G) the build menu

      (M) the map

      (J) this journal

      (T) the newest tutorial

      [E] use whatever is in front of you


      Any of these can be changed under Options, Controls, and this page will follow.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 22db94b9ccae2104aadefa5b986d4c37, type: 3}
    summary: Everything you carry, make and know has a window of its own, each on its own key.
  - group: Getting about
    title: Your Journal
    line: It fills in as you go
    body: 'A dot marks anything you haven''t read yet, and a tab''s count shows how many of them it holds.


      A creature''s page starts with little more than its name. It fills in as they fall: first how it fights and what it leaves, then how to live through it (being killed by one teaches you that too), and last what is told of it. People you bring home add what they know.


      Searching caches in a raid can turn up lost pages, which go in Backstory. Raids keeps a record of how each one ended.


      On Quests you can pin a quest to the top of your tracker and, at home, go straight to where it wants you.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 242e9835e13c1fe4d8de161e7692ec81, type: 3}
    summary: 'The journal keeps what you learn: the story so far, your quests, the creatures you have met and how things work.'
  - group: Getting about
    title: Sneaking
    line: Quiet, slow and worth it
    body: 'Hold Left Ctrl to sneak: half speed, quiet and hard to see. A hit on a creature that hasn''t noticed you is an ambush, worth half again as much.


      Creatures notice you three ways. They see in a cone in front of them, and cover blocks it. They sense what is very close. And they hear, so running, fighting, chopping and picking locks all carry. Rain muffles you. A heavy bag doesn''t.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cada299a42945b04b8c891d31b0c5351, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 73168179ecadba64aa0f05aa045be5e0, type: 3}
    summary: Moving slowly and quietly so the forest's creatures don't notice you, and striking first when they haven't.
  - group: Gathering
    title: Woodcutting
    line: Fell it, then work it where it lies
    body: 'Walk up to a tree with an axe and hold the attack button, or [E], to raise it. Let go to swing. A glint at the top of the backswing is the perfect moment: let go then for a critical blow. Inside the yellow zone is a sound blow. Too early or too late is a glancing blow, and wears the axe.


      Criticals in a row build a combo that widens the perfect moment, and each one adds a log when the tree comes down.


      The last blow fells the tree. Then the work moves to the ground: take the branches off for sticks, and cut the trunk into sections from the butt up, each one more logs.


      On a raid every swing is heard. Chop too long in one place and the forest grows angry, and sends something to see what the noise is.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a277ba53f2eae0648aa06826e44cbfd8, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0c0b7be86e94b4b4a971fc035b8fe418, type: 3}
    summary: Cut trees with an axe for logs and sticks. Well-timed swings bring down more wood.
  - group: Gathering
    title: Mining
    line: Read the rock and strike true
    body: 'Hold the attack button, or [E], at a rock to raise your pickaxe, and let go to strike. Let go at the glint for a critical blow, inside the yellow zone for a sound one. Glancing blows wear the pick.


      Criticals in a row widen the perfect moment, and every critical adds ore when the rock breaks.


      Ore comes in tiers: copper first, then iron, then moonsilver and the stranger stones of the deep woods. A pick below a rock''s tier is slow going.


      On a raid the ring of a pick carries a long way. Mine too long in one place and the forest sends something to find out why.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e9528bdd6784e9d4eaa85d8753dfa51c, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 33eef5039153005419ad83faba57856e, type: 3}
    summary: Break rock and ore with a pickaxe. Better ore needs a better pick.
  - group: Gathering
    title: Foraging
    line: Berries, herbs, fibre and mushrooms
    body: 'Press [E] at a plant to pick it by hand. It takes a moment, and a better Foraging skill makes it quicker.


      Some plants are cut with a sickle instead, with the same swing as an axe: hold to raise, let go at the glint.


      Berries and mushrooms are food, herbs go into salves and draughts, and nettle and flax become cloth and cord.


      Foraging is quiet work, the safest there is on a raid.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4fde8ce0d82ef0d42b6bc607ec3f9a7a, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: de00f5232f0e6fc439112f1356d4e8e6, type: 3}
    summary: Pick plants by hand, or cut them with a sickle, for food, medicine and cloth.
  - group: Gathering
    title: Fishing
    line: Patience, then a fight
    body: 'With a rod in hand, hold the attack button to raise it and swing it back, then let go to cast. Each cast takes one bait from your bag: grubs from rotten logs and stumps, or berries.


      Wait for the float to go under, then strike. Now the fight is on: hold to reel in, let go to give line. When the fish runs to one side, lean the rod against it with the movement keys.


      Too much tension for too long and the line snaps. Too much slack and a fresh fish throws the hook. Steady pressure tires it, and a tired fish at the bank is yours.


      Different fish bite in still water and in rivers. And in still water, not everything that bites is a fish.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b7b0a5e2ce2709341b1d81708498a315, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4bfbc7941652ae6459908fec8bfee9d1, type: 3}
    summary: Catch fish with a rod and bait. Landing one is a tug of war you win by being steady.
  - group: Combat
    title: Swings and Chains
    line: Patience beats clicking
    body: 'Tap the left mouse button for a light swing. Press again after it has landed and you go on to the next swing of the weapon''s chain, and the last one is a finisher: wider, harder and better at breaking poise.


      Pressing right as a swing recovers is on the rhythm, a small edge in damage. Swings never get faster, so mashing gains nothing.


      Hold the button and the swing turns heavy: slow, nearly rooted, and hard enough to break poise. Keep holding to charge it, then let go to strike.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7c67b2279454d4b408f27add06b9e25b, type: 3}
    summary: Your weapon's attacks come as a chain of swings, and timing matters more than speed.
  - group: Combat
    title: Guard and Parry
    line: Part of a blow, or none of it
    body: 'Hold the right mouse button to guard. It stops blows from the front, but part of each still gets through (a lot with bare fists, much less with a shield) and each block costs stamina. Run out and your guard breaks, and you reel for over a second.


      Raise the guard just before a blow lands and it is a parry: no damage, no stamina, the attacker staggers and your next swing is a sure critical. A creature''s warning on the ground turns pale and the creature glints at exactly that moment.


      Lowering your guard locks it for a moment, so tapping it is no free parry.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 93da85e4e0d667b41a6deb8751bb1fcc, type: 3}
    summary: A guard takes part of a blow. A guard raised at the last moment takes none of it and opens the attacker up.
  - group: Combat
    title: Dodging
    line: Your way out of almost anything
    body: 'Space dodges. A dodge can cut a swing short at any time, though during the wind-up that swing is lost and its stamina spent.


      Dodging through a blow as it lands is a perfect dodge, and readies a counter. With an enemy in focus, a dodge steered towards or past it curves around to the spot behind it.


      What you wear decides how you dodge. Light gear gives a short, cheap quickstep, normal gear a roll, and heavy gear a slow shoulder charge that barges enemies at the end.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: aaacc12f67da1d34384aa499ec5f4489, type: 3}
    summary: A quick roll or step out of harm's way, and the surest way out of a bad spot.
  - group: Combat
    title: Stamina and Focus
    line: One holds you up, the other pays for skills
    body: 'Stamina runs everything physical and comes back quickly once you stop spending it. Watch it: an empty bar in the middle of a fight is how most people die.


      Focus, the gold bar, is earned by fighting well. Every hit adds some, a perfect dodge more and a parry most of all. It holds for ten seconds after your last gain, then drains. Skills and weapon arts cost Focus, so they are what good fighting buys and not what opens a fight.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 97a1cd59086df964295e568fcf764acc, type: 3}
    summary: 'Two bars run a fight: stamina for everything you do, Focus for your abilities.'
  - group: Combat
    title: Poise and Stagger
    line: The thin amber bar
    body: 'Every hit wears down a creature''s poise, the thin amber bar under its health. Heavy swings, finishers and counters wear it most. At zero it staggers: its attack is cancelled, it reels, and it takes more damage. A parry staggers it too.


      Poise comes back after a couple of seconds without being hit, so keep at it.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3ec88d50adef5e849a6e644c1b950c1d, type: 3}
    summary: Wear a creature down and it staggers, open to your best blows.
  - group: Combat
    title: Backstabs and Finishing Blows
    line: The best blow there is
    body: 'A pale wedge on the ground shows the spot behind an enemy. A staggered enemy struck from there takes a sure critical at far more damage: that is the best blow in the game. So parry, roll behind, strike.


      A backstab straight out of a dodge gives back half of what the dodge cost.


      Behind a staggered person-shaped creature, such as a draug, a press locks you together for a finishing blow, and nothing can knock you out of it before the blade lands.


      Enemies learn. One that has taken a backstab, or seen one nearby, starts to see the next coming, and the wedge warms from pale to red as it does. It forgets given time. Great beasts and elites are only ever open while staggered.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c4d1a7d56cb31d8409bdd56417434419, type: 3}
    summary: Striking a staggered enemy from behind is the strongest blow there is.
  - group: Combat
    title: Getting Hit
    line: Don't trade blows
    body: 'A hit that gets through while you wind up costs you the swing and leaves you reeling. Trading blows with a monster is a losing game, unless you are swinging something heavy: the wind-up of a heavy swing pushes through hits with a hammer, maul, greatsword or two-handed axe.


      Some attacks leave something behind if they get through. Poison drains your health and an Antidote cures it. Chill slows you and a Warming Brew cures it. Roots hold you in place, though you can still fight.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 98481e79d59499846a4c2d233cfe5948, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a801f1ab35ac02f41aca7387aef7936a, type: 3}
    summary: What happens when a blow gets through, and why trading hits is a losing game.
  - group: Combat
    title: Archery
    line: Draw, breathe, release
    body: 'With a bow in hand, hold the attack button to draw and let go to loose. The arrow flies at the creature nearest your aim, outlined in red. A part draw is weaker, slower and less accurate.


      Let go just as the draw fills for a perfect release: a sure critical that flies true. In a fight the guard button aims instead of guarding: slower, but steadier.


      After a perfect dodge the next press looses an instant counter shot, even while reloading. A creature that hasn''t noticed you takes an ambush bonus from an arrow too.


      Arrows are used up, so bring enough.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c02bc5ecd6589b94daa2ae6d5320cfb6, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6e8443e0fad678943bef5c172ef7d827, type: 3}
    summary: Shoot arrows with a bow. A full draw, let go at the right moment, hits hardest.
  - group: Combat
    title: Abilities
    line: What Focus is for
    body: 'Your abilities are in the skill book (K). Drag one onto the bar to use it, and press (1) to (5) to use what is in each slot.


      An ability costs Focus, the gold bar you earn by fighting well, and stamina, and then has to cool down before it can be used again.


      New abilities come from rune books. At the altar, Purified Essence deepens the ones you know.


      Every spell you cast trains Runecraft, and a better Runecraft makes them hit harder.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0bf8c75e4c32304428c7000e1e01913b, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d03cfd5169e5ca240a4efca33f4f72f5, type: 3}
    summary: Abilities are strong moves and spells on keys 1 to 5, paid for with Focus and stamina.
  - group: Raids
    title: Setting Out
    line: What you decide at the portal
    body: 'The portal''s planner shows where you can go and what you will meet. You choose a destination and a tier, and can pay Portal Sparks for more time (three minutes each, up to two) and carry runes that change what waits on the other side.


      Each raid has a reason, usually a rumour pointing you at something worth finding. The woods are laid out anew every time, so nothing is where you left it.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2614c1d189f3a034691f98f3d3efeee0, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 47081b5d7f0750b4ca34505de73bc596, type: 3}
    summary: A raid is a trip through the portal into the forest, to find what the Haven needs and bring it home.
  - group: Raids
    title: The Clock and the Way Out
    line: Leave before it closes
    body: 'A raid runs on a clock. As it runs down the woods grow more dangerous in stages, and the way home narrows.


      To leave you have to reach an exit, light it and hold it until it opens. Holding takes time and can draw attention, so light one with time to spare.


      The map (M) and the way line show you where to go.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2614c1d189f3a034691f98f3d3efeee0, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4e65a6e3278530d4c82d1bdd3810c280, type: 3}
    summary: Every raid runs on a clock, and you must reach an exit and get through it before time runs out.
  - group: Raids
    title: What You Can Lose
    line: Before you find out the hard way
    body: 'If you fall or time runs out, you wake at the portal. What you carry is lost: materials, food and anything found in the raid.


      The tools, weapons and packs you bring come back damaged, and can be repaired at home.


      Your safe pocket keeps what is in it no matter what, so put the one thing you can''t bear to lose there. Your home, your storage, your recipes and what you have learned are never at risk from a raid.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2614c1d189f3a034691f98f3d3efeee0, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 99bb56b3d61b2d24580e64220d0475d3, type: 3}
    summary: Falling on a raid costs what you carry. Knowing what is at stake helps you decide what to bring.
  - group: Raids
    title: Carrying It Home
    line: Greed has a weight
    body: 'Materials are items with weight. Past most of your bag''s limit you slow down, tire faster and make more noise, and it gets worse the fuller it is. A Haul Sack carries more, but it is slower and louder still.


      Carts carry far more than you can, and can come through the portal with you, but creatures will raid one left alone.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2614c1d189f3a034691f98f3d3efeee0, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 314f3d943d6c38549afc8ffe5480e69c, type: 3}
    summary: Everything you carry has weight, and a heavy load slows you down.
  - group: Raids
    title: Companions
    line: Company has a price
    body: 'You can take someone with you. They fight beside you and take orders in conversation: follow, stay, defend, retreat or attack your target.


      If they fall, they may be lost to the forest, and it will start to forget them. You can find them again, but it takes a rumour and a raid to do it, and they may not remember everything when they come home.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 08ed06b5fb8d1854c86788aa2a00156f, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d9fea10ab2d58cf4f837866b9dc87a21, type: 3}
    summary: Someone from the Haven can come with you on a raid, at a risk.
  - group: Safe Haven
    title: The Ward and Renown
    line: Why a bigger home is a safer one
    body: 'The portal''s ward is what keeps the clearing peaceful. Everything you build and clear adds renown, and renown raises the Haven''s rank, which widens the ward and lights the way a little further for anyone still out there.


      The Haven window (H) shows what counts, what to do next and how far along you are.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f89173a9aeb790c4f9aeb1cc56e0e655, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 60a0b7c0a0b81d44cb1c5ddcaf53ba18, type: 3}
    summary: The portal's ward keeps the clearing safe, and it grows as the Haven grows.
  - group: Safe Haven
    title: Building
    line: Each thing opens the next
    body: 'Press (G) to build inside the ward. Most buildings go up as a scaffold you hammer with [E]. Each one opens the next, and every tier of a building opens something new to make, takes a chore off your hands or answers a problem you will meet in the woods.


      Recipes you can''t make yet still show at the station, with what they need, so you can see what to aim for.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 71d286514cbbbe149ba663b354b4f1ae, type: 2}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b8881e57aaf87664791862c7672142d4, type: 3}
    summary: Raise new buildings inside the ward. Each one opens new things to make and do.
  - group: Safe Haven
    title: Stations and Work
    line: It goes on without you
    body: 'Stations keep working while you are away. Pay on queuing, leave for a raid, and come back to a finished output slot. Crops on a Farm Plot grow the same way.


      Give someone a job from the Haven window and they make things from what is in your stash while you are gone. People want somewhere to sleep, and beds help them, but beds are never what stops you from growing.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f89173a9aeb790c4f9aeb1cc56e0e655, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 53ba481bb31f8fb4fa92e183265ef1c9, type: 3}
    summary: Crafting stations work while you are away, and your people can work them for you.
  - group: Safe Haven
    title: Nights and Breaches
    line: Safe, but not perfectly
    body: 'After the first breach is won, weak creatures prowl just outside the light at night, so keep your fires lit. Cursed Essence is richer after dark too, if you want to go looking.


      Now and then something tests the ward. A breach is always announced ahead of time: you get a warning, time to prepare, the defence itself and a chance to recover. It only happens while you are there, and it can''t wipe out the home you have built. Damaged buildings can be repaired.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fea0201f13773f04a96efbcb5b364ea9, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 69ad07a97c5115840a66eae67d0d706a, type: 3}
    summary: Night brings creatures to the edge of the light, and now and then something tests the ward.
  - group: Safe Haven
    title: The Haven's Reach
    line: Light the stones, then hold the land
    body: 'Claiming. Find one of a region''s named places (walk up to it and it goes on your map (M)), then use its boundary stone [E]. The first stone answers to your fire alone; every one after wants a Pact Rune. Runes turn up in supply caches on raids, and at the rot''s heart.


      Holding. A held region has a hold from 0 to 100. It starts at 40 and wears a little at every turn (each dawn at home, and the end of each raid), faster under blight. Below 25 it is slipping, from 70 it is Secure, and at nothing the forest takes it back.


      What firms it: what the region asks now and then (hunting, gathering or fishing there: its stone says which), a Pact Rune offered at its stone (+25), and each of its places you find (+5).


      The forest pushes back. Now and then it gathers against the weakest of your lands, and two turns later pushes in and takes about 30 hold. Stand watch at that region''s stone (what the forest sends comes for it: beat it all without straying) to break the push, or burn the rot''s heart on a raid: each heart halves it. Or let it come.


      What it gives. Every held region adds renown. A Secure one sends its goods to the stash at every dawn, and the corrupted nights never come from it.


      The Haven window''s Lands tab (H) shows every region, how firmly it is held and what it asks. With friends, the lands are the host''s: a friend can lay runes in the host''s stones, help with what a land asks, and fight beside the host''s watch.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bb2c787a2de76634ba9260ee402850fc, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 61a07dc305b888543bfb5d0879a80e08, type: 3}
    summary: Beyond the meadows the land is split into regions, each with a boundary stone. Light a stone and its region is the Haven's; hold it against the forest and it gives back.
  - group: Keeping going
    title: Hunger and Thirst
    line: They won't kill you
    body: 'Hunger and thirst wear down what you can do, but they never kill you. Berries and a stream will do to start with.


      Cooked meals give timed bonuses on top of what they restore. You can have two at once, and a third pushes out the one closest to ending. Tonics from the Cauldron take no meal slot. Both go through the portal with you, so the meal before a raid counts, but a failed raid loses them.


      Eating stops you for a moment, and a hit that gets through interrupts it, though the food is kept. Its healing arrives over several seconds.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6d70f426af47d0242b7c7793361c6028, type: 3}
    summary: You need to eat and drink to stay at your best, and a good meal does more than fill you.
  - group: Keeping going
    title: Skills and Perks
    line: Getting better at it
    body: 'Every skill grows by doing it. Swing an axe and Woodcutting grows, land blows and Melee grows, cook and Cooking grows. Work done on a raid counts half again, but that share only comes home if you do.


      Every ten levels a skill reaches a milestone and you choose one of two perks. You can choose again at home, beside the portal.


      Quests, raids, first crafts, catches and new places give Insight instead. Put it into any skill you like at (N).


      A skill grows faster once its mentor building at home is upgraded, and after a good night''s sleep.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5cc9278b6487dbc43a5261fd3732c42b, type: 3}
    summary: 'You get better at what you do: thirteen skills, from Woodcutting to Runecraft, each with its own level and perks.'
  - group: Keeping going
    title: Essence
    line: What the forest leaves behind
    body: 'Cursed Essence comes from the forest and its creatures. Purify it at the altar and Purified Essence will empower your gear, enchant it and deepen your skills.


      Every offer at the altar says what it costs and what it does, and none of them can fail or waste your essence. Where there is a risk, it is a stated price.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e9a34a9ca91ab4946b93ffe90aebd8c1, type: 2}
    unlockedByCreature: {fileID: 0}
    unlockedByResident: {fileID: 0}
    foundInRaids: 0
    unlockedBySkill: {fileID: 0}
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ad682811bacef654688bf3f0c8496e03, type: 3}
    summary: Cursed Essence comes from the forest. Purified at the altar, it makes your gear and skills stronger.
  - group: Getting about
    title: Horses
    line: A rope, barley, and a seat kept
    body: 'Wild horses graze in the land round the Haven. Come close crouched: a walk is heard ten metres off. With a lasso in hand, throw it from within its reach (the attack button).


      On the rope it fights: tap E or left click, and lean away from it with the movement keys (that costs your breath). Tire it before the rope slips, then get on its back.


      Breaking it in, it veers and bucks: steer against it to keep your seat. When it tosses its head, give it barley (E). Fed enough, it is yours.


      Each horse has its nature: calm, skittish, stubborn or bold. Feed it, groom it once a day and ride it, and it grows fond of you: more stamina, less panic, and it comes when you whistle (X). Saddles carry its bags; barding keeps blows off.


      A Stable keeps horses safe at night and mends them. A mare and a stallion stabled together, both fond of you, may foal. Deep water it swims, on its stamina.


      Something else lives in the bog, and comes out at dusk.'
    unlockedByQuest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e9a34a9ca91ab4946b93ffe90aebd8c1, type: 2}
